CAMEL-18718.description:
Lets see if we can use graalvm-sdk or graalvm-js that can compile and execute javascript code (with npm modules imported)

A dirty prototype

{code}
public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {

        String src = "import {faker} from '../js/node_modules/@faker-js/faker/dist/esm/index.mjs';" +
                     "const randomName = faker.name.fullName();" +
                     "console.log(randomName);";
    
        Context cx = Context.newBuilder("js")
                    .allowIO(true)
                    .build();
    
        cx.eval(Source.newBuilder("js", src, "test.mjs").build());
    }
{code}

If we can then make this as a language in Camel then end users can more easily use this together with Camel.

CAMEL-18940.description:
The Vert.x web router has built-in support for path & query parameters. We could leverage this on the WS server consumer for vertx-websocket and have path params propagated as Camel headers. E.g  with a route configured like:

from("vertx-websocket:localhost:8080/chat/{user}")
.log("${header.user} >>> ${body}");
